  "slug": "basal-ganglia-29a7",
  "summary": "Four Cell papers on 12 Nov 2026 report multimodal and population-scale brain atlases, with human basal ganglia and striatum central.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is single-cell mapping of regulatory layers and expression variation in the brain, with basal ganglia and striatum as focal tissues. Cell papers pair histone marks, accessibility, methylation or 3D genome with transcriptomes: eight human basal ganglia regions, 18 adult human brain regions, and 2.5M adult mouse nuclei. Two add deep-learning models, one predicting from sequence and one for variant effects. A striatal snRNA-seq study of 3.9M nuclei from 178 donors quantifies abundance and expression variation with age and common eQTLs. Related preprints extend to a prefrontal cortex multi-omic QTL atlas of 231 donors, harmonized mouse sc/snRNA-seq metadata, and spatial mapping of axon-dendrite interfaces. New is the combination of joint epigenomic profiling with sequence-based modeling and donor-scale variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
